---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Guides">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <a href="/" class="text-xs text-slate-500 hover:text-oxblood-700">← Back to docs</a>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Guides</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600">
      Onboarding tutorials, common workflows, integration patterns. The guide pages migrate from
      the repository's <span class="font-mono">docs/</span> tree in subsequent doc-site releases;
      until then, the canonical references are linked below.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-api/tree/main/docs/architecture"
          class="text-oxblood-700 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Architecture overview</a
        >
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-slate-500">
          System shape, layers, request lifecycle, lifecycle event dispatcher, scheduled jobs.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-api/blob/main/docs/architecture/api-versioning.md"
          class="text-oxblood-700 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">API versioning</a
        >
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-slate-500">
          What's additive vs breaking, deprecation cycle, when /v2/* would ship.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-api/blob/main/docs/api/webhook-events.md"
          class="text-oxblood-700 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Webhook events catalog</a
        >
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-slate-500">
          Per-event-type payload shape, signature verification, retry policy.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-api/blob/main/docs/architecture/team-roles-taxonomy.md"
          class="text-oxblood-700 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Team roles taxonomy</a
        >
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-slate-500">
          Owner / admin / member / viewer; what each role can do in the dashboard.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-slate-500">
      First-party in-doc-site versions of these guides land in subsequent V-NNN releases.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
